---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="About - Johannes Roth">
  <header class="page-header">
    <h1 class="page-title">About</h1>
  </header>

  <section class="section">
    <p>
      I'm a <strong>machine learning engineer and PhD researcher</strong> based in Leipzig.
      My work spans production computer vision, large-scale data processing, and computational neuroscience.
    </p>
    <p>
      At the Max Planck Institute for Human Cognitive and Brain Sciences and University of Giessen,
      I study vision models and their relationship to human brain activity. My research combines model
      evaluation, experimental design, and fMRI studies. I also develop research software and public data services.
    </p>
    <p>
      Previously, I worked on computer vision at CHECK24, medical machine learning, e-commerce product matching,
      and cloud data infrastructure. I'm <strong>available from January 2027</strong> for ML engineering,
      applied data science, and research engineering roles.
    </p>
    <a href="/cv.pdf" download="Johannes_Roth_CV.pdf" class="download-cv">
      <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
        <path d="M21 15v4a2 2 0 0 1-2 2H5a2 2 0 0 1-2-2v-4"/>
        <polyline points="7 10 12 15 17 10"/>
        <line x1="12" y1="15" x2="12" y2="3"/>
      </svg>
      Download CV
    </a>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <h2 class="section-title">The Path</h2>
    <div class="timeline">
      <div class="timeline-item">
        <span class="timeline-date">2022 - Present</span>
        <h3 class="timeline-title">PhD Researcher - Computational Cognitive Neuroscience</h3>
        <p class="timeline-org">Max Planck Institute for Human Cognitive and Brain Sciences & University of Giessen</p>
        <p class="timeline-description">
          Independent research on vision models and human brain activity. Developed methods for model
          evaluation and experimental design, GPU-based data pipelines, and research software for LAION-fMRI
          and re:vision. Supervised working students and interns.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="timeline-item">
        <span class="timeline-date">2021 - 2022</span>
        <h3 class="timeline-title">Research Assistant - ML in Medicine</h3>
        <p class="timeline-org">ScaDS.AI Dresden/Leipzig</p>
        <p class="timeline-description">
          Developed deep-learning models for brain-tumor segmentation, including a multi-plane UNet++ ensemble,
          and clinical mortality-prediction models with uncertainty estimation.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="timeline-item">
        <span class="timeline-date">2020 - 2021</span>
        <h3 class="timeline-title">Full-Stack Developer</h3>
        <p class="timeline-org">Kimetric UG (Freelance)</p>
        <p class="timeline-description">
          Built <a href="https://hebartlab.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener">hebartlab.com</a> and
          <a href="https://things-initiative.org" target="_blank" rel="noopener">things-initiative.org</a>,
          from client requirements and design through Django development, Linux hosting, and maintenance.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="timeline-item">
        <span class="timeline-date">2019 - 2021</span>
        <h3 class="timeline-title">Data Scientist (Working student)</h3>
        <p class="timeline-org">CHECK24</p>
        <p class="timeline-description">
          Independently designed and deployed a computer-vision service processing 20 million hotel images.
          Prototyped image retrieval, duplicate detection, and image-quality assessment. Reduced
          recommendation-data update time by over 95% through incremental processing.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="timeline-item">
        <span class="timeline-date">2018 - 2019</span>
        <h3 class="timeline-title">Data Scientist & Analyst (Working student)</h3>
        <p class="timeline-org">Webdata Solutions (now Vistex) · Mercateo (now Unite)</p>
        <p class="timeline-description">
          Image retrieval pipelines, product classification models, cloud data warehousing (AWS).
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="timeline-item">
        <span class="timeline-date">2014 - 2021</span>
        <h3 class="timeline-title">B.Sc. Business Information Systems & M.Sc. Computer Science</h3>
        <p class="timeline-org">Leipzig University</p>
        <p class="timeline-description">
          B.Sc. (2014–2017), grade 1.5; M.Sc. (2017–2021), grade 1.2. Focused on ML, data analysis, and medical image processing.
          Thesis on using GANs to synthesize images that maximally activate specific brain regions.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Get in Touch</h2>
    <p>
      Happy to chat about research, potential collaborations, or opportunities.
      <a href="mailto:johannes@roth24.de">Email</a> is best. Also on
      <a href="https://linkedin.com/in/johannes-roth-a67baa141" target="_blank" rel="noopener">LinkedIn</a>,
      <a href="https://github.com/andropar" target="_blank" rel="noopener">GitHub</a>,
      <a href="https://huggingface.co/andropar" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Hugging Face</a>, and
      <a href="https://scholar.google.com/citations?user=U3Z3J2gAAAAJ" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Google Scholar</a>.
    </p>
  </section>
</Layout>

<style>
  .download-cv {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: var(--space-sm);
    margin-top: var(--space-xl);
    padding: var(--space-sm) var(--space-lg);
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.8125rem;
    font-weight: 500;
    color: var(--color-text);
    background: transparent;
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    border-radius: 0;
    text-decoration: none;
    transition: all var(--transition-base);
  }

  .download-cv:hover {
    background: var(--color-text);
    color: var(--color-bg);
    border-color: var(--color-text);
  }

  .download-cv svg {
    flex-shrink: 0;
  }

</style>
